<pre class='metadata'>
Title: Better `std::underlying_type` (and LWG4634)
Shortname: D4469
Revision: 0
!Draft Revision: 1
Audience: WG21
Status: D
Group: WG21
Editor: Arthur O'Dwyer, arthur.j.odwyer@gmail.com
URL:
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes, biblio yes, markup yes
Abstract:
  There are unfortunate inconsistencies in how core and library clauses handle
  "underlying type," leading to (1) vendor divergence and (2) difficulties in
  specifying new features such as [[P3643]] `to_signed`. We propose a small
  breaking change to make `std::underlying_type_t<T>` always return the underlying
  type of enums and character types, and to make `std::make_signed_t<T>` always
  operate in terms of `underlying_type_t` instead of playing by its own rules.
Date: 2026-11-09
</pre>

